"notes": "Modified cash basis school district; all funds governmental (school nutrition and activities are special revenue funds in Exhibit D). Top-level receipts/disbursements use Exhibit D (p7) Total Major Governmental Funds column. Printed Exhibit D total receipts 5,888,176; the Local Sources line (2,658,140) is split by account using the fund schedules (Exhibit F-L) and Exhibit B (p5) with computed sums; local, county, state, federal and other subtotals reconcile to Exhibit D. State sources split into General Fund 2,454,525, Special Building 9,610, Nutrition 842. Sale of Property 234 and Insurance Proceeds 153,792 (6,952 GF + 146,840 Special Building) are other financing sources on Exhibit D, so they are in other_financing; the General Fund schedule (Exhibit F) counts 234 and 6,952 inside its receipts, so in detail they appear as revenue lines (sale of assets / reimbursements). Transfers 175,000 in and out are interfund (General to Employee Benefit 60,000, Nutrition 65,000, Activities 50,000) and net to zero; Exhibit F disbursements exclude the 175,000 transfer, so no hidden transfer. Exhibit D nutrition local reads 29,538 (interest 258 + lunch 29,280) to reconcile with Exhibit H. Detail: schedules Exhibit F-L (budget and actual) recorded; no per-object GF schedule exists, so GF spending is function level (not itemized). Exhibit A balance sheet has no liabilities. Pages 1-3 are MD&A (not used). Read pages 1-15 of 15"
